Observed at 399e52e: 0 review items. At 330d409 (main) AND at a570deb: 1 item, the live unwaited assertion.
Same silent drop at 399e52e for these starts before the same assertion: `if (flag) /"/.test(s);`, `else /"/.test(s);`, `const list = [.../"/];`.

Cause: lexicalScopes' regex-start heuristic (scripts/transient-state.mjs:271-279; prev-char set "=(:,;!&|?{}[]~+*%^<>-" plus keyword list return|case|throw|yield|await|of|in) does not know typeof|void|delete|new|instanceof|do|else, nor a statement-position "/" after ")". A quote inside such a regex is then read as a string opener, everything after it becomes string content in the mask, and the guard added at :337 (`if (!scopes.code.startsWith("assert.", m.index)) continue`) drops the live assertion. This is nnqj's mechanism surviving for these starts.

Reverse direction, same heuristic: "]" is in the punctuation set, so division is read as a regex start and the REST OF THE LINE is masked. One line, `const half = hits[0] / 2; assert.equal(await page.evaluate(() => window.__status), "ready");` -> 1 item at 330d409 and a570deb, 0 at 399e52e (live assertion hidden). One line, `const half = hits[0] / 2; await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__status === "ready");` + the assertion -> correctly cleared at 330d409/a570deb, but LISTED at 399e52e (the real wait is masked away). So the delta introduces both a false-negative and a false-positive direction; pre-existing nested-template desync (tests/ux-bubble-stage.test.mjs:507) shows the mask also flips on nested backticks.

Expected: the guard's instrument (scopes.code) should not decide executability from a mask that cannot segment regex literals, or the claim should be bounded and the blind spots pinned.

Impact: review list only, and verified ZERO live instances: `node scripts/transient-state.mjs --list` = 487 items at 330d409, 487 at 399e52e, identical file:line set (diff empty, /tmp/x2/base-roster.txt vs /tmp/x2/tip-roster.txt); the exit code is unaffected (scripts/transient-state.mjs:372 runs statusCandidates only when list is true). Filed P3 for that reason; does not block landing.

Test-shape note: tests/transient-state.test.mjs:357 is named "...regex literals never hide later live status assertions (voicebox-beads-nnqj)" but pins 7 fixtures; none of the shapes above can fail it.

Docs over-claim, unchanged by 399e52e: docs/12-pre-push-gate.md:318 says an executable string-form callback clears the item; a concatenated or variable-held callback still does not (`page.waitForFunction('window.__status === ' + JSON.stringify("ready"))`, or `const s = 'window.__status === "ready"'; waitForFunction(s)` are listed at 330d409 and 399e52e). Zero in-repo instances.

